    {
      "id": 4,
      "name": "Torrent swarm",
      "description": "Whether qBittorrent is actually talking to the swarm, which is a different claim from the tunnel being up and from the pod being ready. It went down for a day with both of those green, because the client had bound to eth0 and the killswitch was silently dropping everything it sent. This is the monitor that would have caught it. Down while the torrent stack is switched off, which is not a fault.",
